WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
If you wanted to write tests for Django, know that you need to use a separate test case

00:06.000 --> 00:13.000
class, not the one that comes in the standard library with Python, but instead use Django.test

00:13.000 --> 00:23.000
test case, and there's guides for running Django tests right here in the course website.

00:23.000 --> 00:29.000
And before we talk about the final, actually I'll give you an overview of the final project practice,

00:29.000 --> 00:36.000
and then we will wrap up, and you will be done with a brain cramped full of Python knowledge.

00:36.000 --> 00:43.000
For the final project practice, you're going to make sure that you're all set up, and then you're going to do a few things.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.000
We're going to sort in reverse order.

00:47.000 --> 00:55.000
So if you saw earlier our blog posts are in chronological order, which is not what we want.

00:55.000 --> 01:00.000
We want them to sort in reverse so that the newest posts are first.

01:00.000 --> 01:09.000
We're also going to add a new is draft fields so that we can have some posts that we're working on, but we don't want to display it.

01:09.000 --> 01:14.000
And then we're also going to write or examine some unit tests.

01:14.000 --> 01:18.000
And there's some links here for going further with Django.

